---
import TileGroup from "../TileGroup.astro";
---
<TileGroup id="expAgurotech" layout="alternative" class="my-25">
    <span slot="title" class="text-4xl max-[1050px]:text-2xl font-semibold font-titles">
        <a href="https://agurotech.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-text">Agurotech</a>
    </span>

    <img
        slot="media"
        src="/media/icons/companies/agurotech.png"
        alt="Agurotech"
        class="w-[50%] h-auto transition-transform duration-300 hover:scale-105 rounded-2xl"
    />

    <Fragment slot="secondary">
        <span class="text-xl font-bold block mb-3">Role & Experience</span>
        <span class="text-lg block mb-1">Fullstack app development</span>
        <p class="text-sm mb-3 font-light text-justify">
            Contributed across the complete tech stack at Amsterdam-based ag-tech startup <a href="https://agurotech.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-text">Agurotech</a>.
            Focused on fullstack mobile/web app with a <a href="https://go.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-text">Golang</a> backend,
            cross-platform frontend UI in <a href="https://flutter.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-text">Flutter</a>,
            serving all from <a href="https://cloud.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-text">Google Cloud</a>.
            Worked with system's <a href="https://www.mongodb.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-text">MongoDB</a>, and <a href="https://firebase.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-text">Firebase</a>.
        </p>
        <span class="text-lg block mb-1">Website rebuild</span>
        <p class="text-sm font-light text-justify">
            Around 2 months into the internship got tasked with rebuilding the companies existing Wordpress website using a modern tech stack.
            Mainly used <a href="https://payloadcms.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-text">Payload CMS</a> which in itself included (<a href="https://react.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-text">React</a>, <a href="https://tailwindcss.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-text">Tailwind</a> and <a href="https://nextjs.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-text">Next.js</a>).
        </p>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="description">
        <span class="text-2xl font-semibold">Agurotech Internship</span>
        <p class="text-sm mt-5 font-light text-justify">
            During my last year of studies in the Netherlands, I landed an internship at <a href="https://agurotech.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-text">Agurotech</a>,
            an innovative agricultural technology startup headquartered in Amsterdam.
            Agurotech builds integrated hardware and software solutions for precision agriculture-combining proprietary soil moisture sensors,
            microclimate weather stations, and telemetry nodes with data-driven mobile and web applications to help farmers make intelligent,
            data-backed irrigation and crop management decisions.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm mt-5 font-light text-justify">
            Joining the team initially as a frontend focused developer, I eventually got to work across the stack in multiple different project.
            It gave me the opportunity to dive deep into real-world, production-scale software development.
            Rather than confining myself to a single slice of the codebase, I worked end-to-end across both cloud infrastructure and client-facing interfaces.
            I got to develop existing system's conforming to coding standards/structures and also build a project from zero in my own vision, being able to make design decisions on my own.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm mt-5 font-light text-justify">
            On the backend, I worked extensively with <a href="https://go.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-text">Golang</a>,
            it was here that I genuinely fell in love with Go-its minimalist philosophy. With its effortless concurrency primitives with <a href="https://go.dev/tour/concurrency/1" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-text">goroutines</a>,
            and blistering execution speed resonated deeply with my passion for systems-level programming.
            This enthusiasm directly influenced future independent projects, including the backend architecture for this portfolio website.
            On the client side, I built and improved cross-platform features using <a href="https://flutter.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-text">Flutter</a> which
            I will always consider a back-pocket framework I can rely on in the future.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm mt-5 font-light text-justify">
            Next to this a project I was tasked was to develop the companies existing <a href="https://wordpress.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-text">WordPress</a> website from zero, using a more modern tech-stack.
            Funnily enough I was tasked with this project due to my previous experience in web development with this portfolio website.
            With the project I got to deepen my knowledge of web development in client side and server side generation (<a href="https://nextjs.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-text">Next.js</a>), learn modern dynamic frameworks like <a href="https://react.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-text">React</a> and internal content management systems like <a href="https://payloadcms.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-text">Payload CMS</a>.
            Gained more knowledge of company wide SEO, cookies and analytics (<a href="https://ads.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-text">Google Ads</a> and <a href="https://analytics.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-text">Google Analytics</a>) which I will deeply value in future work.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm mt-5 font-light text-justify">
            Operating independently in a fast-moving startup environment proved to be invaluable in agile development, code reviews,
            and building software with tangible environmental and economic impact.
            It bridged the gap between existing knowledge from project and the discipline of shipping robust, scalable software in industry.
        </p>
    </Fragment>
</TileGroup>
